---
layout: base.njk
title: "GSVIEC - Bare-metal Automation & Web3 Node Infrastructure"
description: "Bare-metal automation and Web3 node infrastructure for validators, DePIN projects, and enterprise blockchain teams that need control, performance, and uptime."
schema: '{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"Organization","name":"GSVIEC","alternateName":"Global Solutions for Virtualized Infrastructure & Enterprise Computing","url":"https://gsviec.com","logo":"https://gsviec.com/assets/logo-gsviec.png","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Thu Duc City","addressRegion":"Ho Chi Minh City","addressCountry":"VN"}},{"@type":"WebSite","name":"GSVIEC","url":"https://gsviec.com"},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What does GSVIEC provide?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"GSVIEC provides bare-metal automation and Web3 node infrastructure for validators, DePIN projects, and enterprise blockchain teams."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does GSVIEC offer a free infrastructure trial?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. GSVIEC avoids free infrastructure trials to reduce abuse risk. The Starter option is open-source automation guidance, while hosted plans are paid with a 14-day refund policy when applicable."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the main value of bare-metal node hosting?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Bare-metal node hosting can reduce dependency on generic cloud platforms and improve control, latency, performance, and infrastructure cost predictability."}}]}]}'
---
<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="hero.eyebrow">{{ site.brandBackronym }}</p>
    <h1 data-i18n="hero.title">Bare-metal automation for Web3 nodes that cannot afford downtime.</h1>
    <p class="hero-lede" data-i18n="hero.lede">GSVIEC helps validators, DePIN projects, and enterprise blockchain teams deploy node infrastructure with dedicated hardware control, repeatable automation, monitoring, and SLA-led operations.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="#consultation" data-i18n="hero.primary">Book a node audit</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="#plans" data-i18n="hero.secondary">View plans</a>
      <button class="button deploy-button" type="button" data-deploy-trigger><i data-lucide="terminal-square"></i><span data-i18n="hero.deploy">Deploy Mode</span></button>
    </div>
    <div class="trust-strip" aria-label="GSVIEC positioning">
      <span data-i18n="trust.engineer">Engineer-to-Engineer</span>
      <span data-i18n="trust.iac">IaC-first</span>
      <span data-i18n="trust.abuse">No free infra abuse</span>
      <span data-i18n="trust.sovereignty">Designed for sovereignty</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="terminal-card" aria-label="GSVIEC node deployment demo" data-tilt>
    <div class="terminal-bar">
      <span></span><span></span><span></span>
      <strong>gsviec/node-automator</strong>
    </div>
    <pre><code data-typewriter>gsviec deploy node \
  --network solana \
  --profile bare-metal-ha \
  --region eu-central \
  --sla 99.9

PXE boot .............. ready
Firmware policy ....... locked
Docker runtime ........ active
Prometheus alerts ..... synced
Failover route ........ standby

Node status: HEALTHY</code></pre>
    <div class="terminal-status">
      <span class="pulse"></span>
      <span data-i18n="terminal.status">Automation pipeline ready for paid onboarding</span>
    </div>
    <div class="signal-stack" aria-hidden="true">
      <span></span>
      <span></span>
      <span></span>
      <span></span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="metrics" aria-label="Strategic metrics">
  <div><strong>50-85%</strong><span data-i18n="metric.cost">Target infra cost reduction vs generic cloud, subject to workload</span></div>
  <div><strong>30-50%</strong><span data-i18n="metric.throughput">Benchmark target for throughput uplift in suitable bare-metal cases</span></div>
  <div><strong>99.9%</strong><span data-i18n="metric.pro">Pro SLA target after paid deployment</span></div>
  <div><strong>99.99%</strong><span data-i18n="metric.enterprise">Enterprise SLA target with redundancy design</span></div>
</section>

<section id="problem" class="section problem-section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="problem.eyebrow">Market Problem</p>
    <h2 data-i18n="problem.title">Web3 infrastructure is too expensive, too abstracted, and too risky when uptime drives revenue.</h2>
    <p data-i18n="problem.copy">Validators and node operators do not only buy servers. They buy continuity, block participation, latency, and confidence that operations will not fail at the worst moment.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="pillar-grid">
    <div><i data-lucide="wallet-cards"></i><strong data-i18n="problem.card1.title">Cloud cost pressure</strong><p data-i18n="problem.card1.copy">Generic cloud is convenient, but high-volume node workloads can become structurally expensive as request, storage, and bandwidth usage grows.</p></div>
    <div><i data-lucide="shield-alert"></i><strong data-i18n="problem.card2.title">Slashing exposure</strong><p data-i18n="problem.card2.copy">Validator downtime can create protocol penalties. GSVIEC positions infrastructure around uptime visibility, failover thinking, and clear SLA boundaries.</p></div>
    <div><i data-lucide="lock-keyhole"></i><strong data-i18n="problem.card3.title">Limited control</strong><p data-i18n="problem.card3.copy">RPC and managed cloud services are fast to start, but teams lose hardware control, tuning depth, and direct ownership of critical operations.</p></div>
    <div><i data-lucide="workflow"></i><strong data-i18n="problem.card4.title">Manual DevOps burden</strong><p data-i18n="problem.card4.copy">Dedicated servers are cheaper but difficult to operate without automation, monitoring, security policy, and engineer-level support.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="services" class="section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="services.eyebrow">Core Infrastructure</p>
    <h2 data-i18n="services.title">A focused stack for node operators, DePIN teams, and enterprise blockchain builders.</h2>
    <p data-i18n="services.copy">The public offer is narrow by design: bare-metal automation, validator operations, private Web3 cloud, and DevOps automation.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="service-grid">
    {% for item in services %}
    <a class="service-card" href="{{ ('/services/' + item.slug + '/') | relativeUrl(page.url) }}">
      <i data-lucide="{{ item.icon }}"></i>
      <span>0{{ loop.index }}</span>
      <h3 data-i18n="service.{{ item.slug }}.title">{{ item.title }}</h3>
      <p data-i18n="service.{{ item.slug }}.summary">{{ item.summary }}</p>
      <small data-i18n="service.{{ item.slug }}.outcome">{{ item.outcome }}</small>
    </a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section id="plans" class="section plans-section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="plans.eyebrow">Commercial Model</p>
    <h2 data-i18n="plans.title">Three offers that turn technical interest into paid infrastructure.</h2>
    <p data-i18n="plans.copy">Pricing below is indicative and should be confirmed after node requirements, chain, region, redundancy, bandwidth, and support level are scoped.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="pricing-grid">
    <article class="pricing-card">
      <span>Starter</span>
      <h3 data-i18n="plans.starter.title">Open-source automation</h3>
      <strong>Free</strong>
      <p data-i18n="plans.starter.copy">Scripts and documentation for technical teams that want to run a node on their own server.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Ansible/Terraform starter repo</li>
        <li>Local or customer-owned server</li>
        <li>Community-driven lead capture</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="button secondary" href="#consultation" data-i18n="plans.starter.cta">Request repo access</a>
    </article>
    <article class="pricing-card featured">
      <span>Pro</span>
      <h3 data-i18n="plans.pro.title">Managed single node</h3>
      <strong>$100-200/node/mo</strong>
      <p data-i18n="plans.pro.copy">Paid node deployment with monitoring, basic support, and a target SLA for early operators.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Automated bare-metal deployment</li>
        <li>Monitoring and uptime reports</li>
        <li>14-day refund policy after upfront payment</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="button primary" href="#consultation" data-i18n="plans.pro.cta">Start Pro scope</a>
    </article>
    <article class="pricing-card">
      <span>Enterprise</span>
      <h3 data-i18n="plans.enterprise.title">Multi-node failover</h3>
      <strong>$500+/mo</strong>
      <p data-i18n="plans.enterprise.copy">Custom topology for validators, DePIN projects, and enterprise blockchain systems.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Multi-node redundancy</li>
        <li>Auto-failover beta path</li>
        <li>24/7 technical support and SLA 99.99% target</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="button secondary" href="#consultation" data-i18n="plans.enterprise.cta">Book enterprise demo</a>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="architecture" class="section split-section">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="architecture.eyebrow">Infrastructure Architecture</p>
    <h2 data-i18n="architecture.title">From physical servers to repeatable Web3 operations.</h2>
    <p data-i18n="architecture.copy">GSVIEC's strategic advantage is the bridge between bare-metal control and software-defined operations. The system should make a dedicated server behave like a disciplined infrastructure product.</p>
    <ul class="check-list">
      <li>PXE boot and automated OS provisioning for fast node setup</li>
      <li>BIOS, firmware, VLAN, and bonding policy for performance control</li>
      <li>Terraform and Ansible scripts for repeatable deployments</li>
      <li>Monitoring, alerts, backup, and failover readiness for uptime</li>
      <li>KYC-light and paid onboarding to reduce abuse risk</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="architecture-panel">
    <div>Customer KYC</div>
    <div>Paid Scope</div>
    <div>Terraform</div>
    <div>Ansible</div>
    <div>PXE Boot</div>
    <div>Node Runtime</div>
    <div>Prometheus</div>
    <div>Failover</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section blockchain-section">
  <div class="blockchain-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="blockchain.eyebrow">Proof of Technical Direction</p>
    <h2 data-i18n="blockchain.title">Open-source scripts create trust; managed operations create revenue.</h2>
    <p data-i18n="blockchain.copy">The Starter repo attracts technical operators. Pro and Enterprise convert teams that need SLA, support, failover, and someone accountable for production readiness.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="blockchain-flow" aria-label="Validator node status">
    <div class="blockchain-card">
      <i data-lucide="box"></i>
      <span>Block #192834</span>
      <strong class="status-validated">Validated</strong>
      <code>hash: 0x8a72...3f9</code>
    </div>
    <div class="blockchain-card">
      <i data-lucide="activity"></i>
      <span>Validator Node</span>
      <strong class="status-validated">Healthy</strong>
      <code>slot_lag: 0</code>
    </div>
    <div class="blockchain-card">
      <i data-lucide="radio-tower"></i>
      <span>Failover Route</span>
      <strong class="status-validated">Standby</strong>
      <code>latency: monitored</code>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="comparison" class="section comparison-section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Competitive Position</p>
    <h2>Between DIY dedicated servers and expensive enterprise node services.</h2>
    <p>GSVIEC should compete on control, support, and price-performance: more accountable than pure DIY, more flexible than RPC-only providers, and more accessible than high-end enterprise vendors.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="comparison-table" role="table" aria-label="Competitive comparison">
    <div role="row" class="table-head"><span>Option</span><span>Strength</span><span>Tradeoff</span><span>GSVIEC angle</span></div>
    <div role="row"><span>Infura / Alchemy</span><span>Fast API access</span><span>No hardware control; volume-based cost</span><span>Better for teams needing owned node operations</span></div>
    <div role="row"><span>Chainstack</span><span>Managed multi-chain access</span><span>Request-based scaling economics</span><span>More control for performance-sensitive workloads</span></div>
    <div role="row"><span>Akash</span><span>Decentralized cloud economics</span><span>Token and stability uncertainty</span><span>SLA-led operating model with technical support</span></div>
    <div role="row"><span>Hetzner / OVH DIY</span><span>Low server cost</span><span>Customer handles all DevOps risk</span><span>Automation, monitoring, and Web3-specific operations</span></div>
    <div role="row"><span>Blockdaemon</span><span>Enterprise node service</span><span>Premium pricing</span><span>Focused middle position for startups and growing infra teams</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section trust-section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Technical Trust Signals</p>
    <h2>What GSVIEC must prove publicly.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="pillar-grid">
    <div><strong>Open-source starter</strong><p>Publish deployment scripts and documentation so technical buyers can inspect the operating model before buying managed service.</p></div>
    <div><strong>Benchmark reports</strong><p>Show workload-specific comparisons for latency, throughput, sync time, and monthly infrastructure cost.</p></div>
    <div><strong>Uptime dashboard</strong><p>Make demo node health visible with uptime, incident notes, and recovery behavior.</p></div>
    <div><strong>SLA clarity</strong><p>State refund, uptime, and slashing-liability boundaries clearly before onboarding paid nodes.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section insights-preview">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Latest Insights</p>
    <h2 data-i18n="insights.title">Engineer-to-engineer content for validators and infrastructure teams.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="post-grid">
    {% for post in collections.posts %}
    {% if loop.index <= 3 %}
    <a class="post-card" href="{{ post.url | relativeUrl(page.url) }}">
      <span>{{ post.data.category }}</span>
      <h3>{{ post.data.title }}</h3>
      <p>{{ post.data.summary }}</p>
      <small>{{ post.data.date | readableDate }}</small>
    </a>
    {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section id="consultation" class="consultation">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="contact.eyebrow">Book a Node Audit</p>
    <h2 data-i18n="contact.title">Find out whether your node workload should move to bare metal.</h2>
    <p data-i18n="contact.copy">Send your chain, region, uptime target, current monthly cost, and whether you need single-node Pro or Enterprise failover. GSVIEC will respond with the next technical step.</p>
  </div>
  <form class="contact-form" action="{{ site.formEndpoint }}" method="POST" data-contact-form>
    <label><span data-i18n="form.name">Full name</span><input name="name" autocomplete="name" required></label>
    <label><span data-i18n="form.email">Work email</span><input type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" required></label>
    <label><span data-i18n="form.company">Project / company</span><input name="company" autocomplete="organization"></label>
    <label><span data-i18n="form.message">Node or infrastructure need</span><textarea name="message" rows="5" placeholder="Network, current provider, monthly cost, uptime target, region, and expected node count" data-i18n-placeholder="form.placeholder" required></textarea></label>
    <button class="button primary" type="submit" data-i18n="form.submit">Request infrastructure audit</button>
    <p class="form-note" data-i18n="form.note">If Formspree is not configured yet, the form opens your email app and sends to hello@gsviec.com.</p>
  </form>
</section>
